  "summary": "Malicious code in strapi-plugin-perev-meeb (npm)",
  "details": "The package's postinstall hook (postinstall.js) runs a reverse shell on install. It checks the machine hostname and, if it matches 'ubuntu-fc-uvm', spawns a python3 reverse shell that connects to 14[.]225[.]210[.]85:80 and hands the remote host an interactive shell (pty.spawn(\"sh\")), retrying up to 5 times. The hostname check is an evasion gate to avoid running in analysis environments.",
